# .mailmap — Git's built-in display-mapping for commit authors.
# Maps historical commit-author identities to the canonical maintainer-identity.
# Does NOT change commit-objects — only how `git log`, `git shortlog`, and
# GitHub's web UI display them.
# Format spec: https://git-scm.com/docs/gitmailmap
#
# Background (Sprint-4/5 Folge, 2026-06-28): Local git config in earlier
# AI-sessions was set to "Codebuff-CI-Validator <ci-validate@swingz.local>",
# which causes Vercel to BLOCK deployments ("commit author email ... is not
# valid. Ensure your git email matches your GitHub account."). The 12 most
# recent Sprint-4/5 commits were rewritten via scripts/_rewrite_sprint45_authors.py
# + force-pushed. Older commits from earlier sessions may still carry the wrong
# identity — this .mailmap displays them as the canonical maintainer everywhere.
#
# CANONICAL MAINTAINER-IDENTITY (single source-of-truth):
#   See `scripts/_maintainer_identity.sh` for the canonical name + email
#   (EXPECTED_NAME / EXPECTED_EMAIL exported there). The entry-rows below
#   hardcode the values because git's `.mailmap` parser is a literal-lookup
#   mechanism with no source/include support — if the maintainer-identity
#   ever changes: (1) update scripts/_maintainer_identity.sh first, (2)
#   mirror the new values in the entry-rows below, (3) re-run husky
#   pre-commit to verify.
#
# Format per row: <wrong-name> <wrong-email> <canonical-name> <canonical-email>

# Sprint-4/5 rewrite (→ historical artifact: 12 commits have backend rewrites)
Bart Mz <bartmz@gmx.de> Codebuff-CI-Validator <ci-validate@swingz.local>
Bart Mz <bartmz@gmx.de> Bart Mz <mike.swinger@gmx.de>

# Earlier AI-session variants (if you encounter these in `git log`, add a row):
# Add more rows here when a new wrong-identity pattern emerges.
# Example template:
# Some AI Name <wrong@email> Bart Mz <bartmz@gmx.de>
